<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka sees tea crop up 2 pct, rubber up 6 pct.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka sees tea crop up 2 pct, rubber up 6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's tea production is forecast to reach 250 million kg this year, up two percent from 1995, Deputy Finance Minister G.L. Peiris said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Tea prices for the first nine months of this year increased by 40 percent compared to the same period last year,&quot; Peiris told parliament as he presented the state budget for calendar 1997.</p>
<p>Rubber production is expected to increase by six percent to 112 million kg this year, he said.</p>
<p>Rubber prices had dropped by 20 percent this year compared to 1995 but were still favourable.</p>
</text>
